"""hacking_355_backtest.py -- Does closing on a 355pm imbal flip improve PnL?

For each strategy (IMBAL_VS_MARKET / IMBAL_GROWS parents + CLOSER variants, plus the
3 prod BUMPED strategies: GROWS / VS_MARKET / SHRINKS):
  Original PnL = held to settlement (current behavior).
  Hacked  PnL = if 355pm imbal flips against trade direction (|imbal_355| > $1B),
                close spread at 15:55:03 OPRA cross (short_ask - long_bid).
                Otherwise keep original PnL.

Fill mode (default, capped): the achievable buy-back price each second is the displayed
cross (short_ask - long_bid, NaN long bid -> 0) PLUS fast-market slippage of
max(SLIP_FLOOR, SLIP_PCT * cross) (defaults $0.20 / 10%; lower via --slip-floor /
--slip-pct). A triggered leg fills only when this slipped price is <= MAX_HACK_COST,
checked at 15:55:03 and then every second through 16:00:00. At 15:55:03 we take the
market: a slipped price already at or under the cap fills at that slipped price. Any
later fill models a resting bid at MAX_HACK_COST getting hit, so it fills at exactly
MAX_HACK_COST. Never under the cap -> leg not hacked (keeps original PnL).
Legacy mode (pass --uncapped on the CLI): always fill at the raw 15:55:03 cross, any
price, no slippage.

Hack size (default): HALF the leg (floor), matching prod's hack_size = size_filled // 2 --
1-lot legs are skipped and the unhacked remainder rides to settlement. --full-size unwinds
100% of the position (the pre-9/2 research behavior).

Incremental mode: --last-days N restricts everything to the last N trading days in the
combined panel (shrinks the OPRA pull to N dates; for the daily task). Absent -> full history.

Flip rule (matches prior 6/8/26 research):
  short Put  + imbal_355 < -$1B  -> hack-close (big sell pressure vs short-put position)
  short Call + imbal_355 > +$1B  -> hack-close (big buy  pressure vs short-call position)

Output xlsx (Downloads):
  Sheet 1 = Summary, Sheets 2+ = per-strategy per-leg detail.
"""

